# Normalization for all contributors, whatever their machine.
#
# Why: this repo is deployed from a Linux DGX, but it is also edited from macOS
# and Windows. Without this rule, a file rewritten under Windows arrives with
# CRLF line endings: `bash -n` then rejects every script, `git diff` shows the
# whole file as modified, and a systemd unit or Dockerfile copied as-is fails
# for a reason invisible to the eye. `text=auto` normalizes in the repo and
# lets Git choose on checkout; images and fonts are explicitly binary,
# otherwise Git "repairs" them by mangling the bytes and corrupts the file.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# The dependency lock is generated: `linguist-generated=true` folds it into
# the diffs and takes it out of the language statistics. On the other hand NO
# `-diff`: it made the file binary for Git, so every version change became
# INVISIBLE in review. Measured on 2026-10-01 on the `brace-expansion` fix: the
# only trace was « Bin 251602 -> 251628 bytes ». Yet a lockfile is precisely
# what a reviewer must see moving — that is where a replaced package or an
# unwanted dependency gets spotted.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# `git archive` (release tarball) does not need the development tooling:
# neither the issue templates, nor the CI, nor the screenshots.
.github/ export-ignore
scripts/ export-ignore
assets/ export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
.dockerignore export-ignore
.editorconfig export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
